exercises.solution:
```python
from fractions import Fraction

def solve_linear(a, b, c, d):
    coeff, rhs = a - c, d - b
    if coeff != 0:
        return Fraction(rhs, coeff)
    return "all" if rhs == 0 else "none"
```

This follows the theorem on $ax = b$ exactly: one solution when the coefficient is non-zero; otherwise the equation reads $0 = d - b$, which is either always true or never true.
